00:22:09,536 --> 00:22:12,664
so as Britney Spears would say,
"You better work, bitch."

480
00:22:13,415 --> 00:22:16,126
Keep up. Cheers to that!

481
00:22:16,209 --> 00:22:17,044
Whoo!

482
00:22:17,127 --> 00:22:18,295
-Cheers.
-Cheers.

483
00:22:22,799 --> 00:22:25,052
-Agh.
-It's burning my chest.

484
00:22:25,135 --> 00:22:27,471
I'm sorry. Do you have a napkin?

485
00:22:27,554 --> 00:22:29,389
Is it-- [chuckles] No.

486
00:22:29,473 --> 00:22:30,766
Oh, gross.

487
00:22:33,477 --> 00:22:35,020
Hi, honey, how are you?

488
00:22:35,103 --> 00:22:36,521
You're young like my man, huh?

489
00:22:37,272 --> 00:22:40,525
[giggles] You guys are both cougars. Rawr.

490
00:22:40,609 --> 00:22:42,903
How long have you guys
even been dating?

491
00:22:42,986 --> 00:22:44,488
-Over a year now.
-Over a year?

492
00:22:44,571 --> 00:22:45,781
Yeah, a bit over a year.

493
00:22:45,864 --> 00:22:48,492
-Twenty-five, right?
-Yes.

494
00:22:48,575 --> 00:22:51,203
Are you an old soul or a young soul?

495
00:22:51,661 --> 00:22:53,955
-I feel like an old one.
-Oh.

496
00:22:54,039 --> 00:22:55,582
-I mean, I know what I want.
-Yeah.

497
00:22:55,665 --> 00:22:57,709
You do? Good for you!

498
00:22:57,793 --> 00:22:59,878
[Chrishell]
Does he really know what he wants at 25?

499
00:22:59,961 --> 00:23:03,090
Hopefully, we'll see,
but... I don't know. [chuckles]

500
00:23:03,173 --> 00:23:05,384
Am I allowed to ask what is that?
No, I won't ask.

501
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:09,096
-Yeah, I wanna hear this. What is that?
-Yeah, why not? What do you want?

502
00:23:11,348 --> 00:23:12,891
Are you guys getting married?

503
00:23:12,974 --> 00:23:14,559
Know what, I thought about it.

504
00:23:19,147 --> 00:23:20,690
Nice to meet you. Hi.

505
00:23:22,150 --> 00:23:23,568
-So where's your husband?
-Miami.

506
00:23:23,652 --> 00:23:25,362
Is he gonna come see you?

507
00:23:25,445 --> 00:23:28,407
Yeah, he couldn't come,
so it sucks you know?

508
00:23:28,490 --> 00:23:30,992
-It's so hard, I know. Trust me, I know.
-It's hard.

509
00:23:31,076 --> 00:23:31,910
It's sad, it's like--

510
00:23:31,993 --> 00:23:34,746
I'm gonna fly next week for two days
and come back here.

511
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:37,499
Yeah, I wish it was that easy
for me to go to Slovakia.

512
00:23:37,582 --> 00:23:40,001
-Have you talked to Nick?
-He texts me early in the morning.

513
00:23:40,085 --> 00:23:43,713
I mean we're like such, like, different,
opposite sides of the world right now.

514
00:23:43,797 --> 00:23:46,383
-Yeah.
-He's like nine hours ahead, so...

515
00:23:46,466 --> 00:23:49,136
-No, we're talking about, uh--
-My boyfriend.

516
00:23:49,219 --> 00:23:52,264
You know, he's overseas,
it's just the time difference with the--

517
00:23:52,347 --> 00:23:55,767
-[Brett] What's going on with that?
-[laughs] Nothing is going on with that.

518
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:57,727
Everything's fine.

519
00:23:57,811 --> 00:23:59,229
Don't give her shade.

520
00:23:59,312 --> 00:24:01,189
You don't know my relationship.

521
00:24:01,273 --> 00:24:02,441
I agree with that.

522
00:24:02,524 --> 00:24:04,025
I don't need your approval
of my boyfriend.

523
00:24:04,109 --> 00:24:06,153
You don't need our approval,
but we have to meet him.

524
00:24:06,236 --> 00:24:08,196
Of course you're gonna meet him.
You guys are my family,

525
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:10,490
-but I also don't need anyone's approval.
-That's all I'm asking.

526
00:24:10,574 --> 00:24:15,036
Okay, that's fair enough,
but I don't care what you say. I love him.

527
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:17,497
-So it's my decision.
-You do care what I say, but okay.

528
00:24:18,582 --> 00:24:21,293
Listen, Brett wants Heather to stay in LA

529
00:24:21,376 --> 00:24:23,545
just because he wants her
to make money for the brokerage.

530
00:24:23,628 --> 00:24:26,590
I don't know why, though.
She's basic, but whatever.

531
00:24:29,217 --> 00:24:31,261
-Wait, what are we talking about?
-Yeah.

532
00:24:31,344 --> 00:24:32,262
Are you okay?

533
00:24:32,345 --> 00:24:35,098
Yeah, I don't like him trying to--
I mean he doesn't know him.

534
00:24:35,182 --> 00:24:37,350
He is the last person
to give relationship--

535
00:24:37,434 --> 00:24:39,811
He has no... He's not married,
never dated,

536
00:24:39,895 --> 00:24:42,272
-like, I don't need relationship--
-It is what it is.

537
00:24:42,689 --> 00:24:44,191
Don't take it personal.

538
00:24:44,274 --> 00:24:45,859
That's why, like, listen,

539
00:24:45,942 --> 00:24:48,403
I'm gonna have your back on that,
because it's like, listen,

540
00:24:48,486 --> 00:24:53,074
that's not fair for you
to micro-analyze your situation.

541
00:24:53,158 --> 00:24:54,993
That's not fair, Brett. I don't think so.

542
00:24:55,076 --> 00:24:58,997
I don't like you, but I don't have to be
your friend to, like, see what's going on

543
00:24:59,080 --> 00:25:01,875
-and realize that's not fair.
-You're not my friend?

544
00:25:01,958 --> 00:25:04,377
-I mean, not yet, bitch, but--
-What?!

545
00:25:04,961 --> 00:25:06,254
Excuse me?

546
00:25:06,922 --> 00:25:08,173
I did nothing to you.

547
00:25:18,516 --> 00:25:23,438
I went through dinner
we had at a restaurant, um...

548
00:25:23,522 --> 00:25:27,692
I was just shocked and hurt, to be honest.

549
00:25:27,776 --> 00:25:31,613
Like, when I thought that you were saying,
"Oh, it's okay for now, like whatever."

550
00:25:31,696 --> 00:25:33,281
I thought that that was...

551
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:35,367
You were on the same page as me.

552
00:25:35,450 --> 00:25:36,952
I think this scared me...

553
00:25:37,327 --> 00:25:41,373
because I'm so in,

554
00:25:41,456 --> 00:25:44,501
like, this relationship
and I want so much out of it,

555
00:25:44,584 --> 00:25:50,257
and I am one year older
and closer to 40.

556
00:25:50,340 --> 00:25:51,341
Can you handle that?

557
00:25:53,677 --> 00:25:56,096
-Yeah, you're scared, right? [chuckles]
-Yeah.

558
00:25:56,846 --> 00:25:57,889
Really scared.

559
00:25:59,307 --> 00:26:00,684
I like being scared.

560
00:26:02,269 --> 00:26:06,439
-♪ Happy birthday to you... ♪
-Mary, Chrishell, get up here.

561
00:26:06,523 --> 00:26:11,903
♪ Happy birthday
Dear Mary and Chrishell ♪

562
00:26:11,987 --> 00:26:15,323
You kind of caught me off guard
when you said you're not my friend.

563
00:26:15,407 --> 00:26:16,783
Like, what did I do to you?

564
00:26:17,492 --> 00:26:18,660
There was a client.

565
00:26:19,244 --> 00:26:21,913
I was helping him look
for a house in the Hills,

566
00:26:21,997 --> 00:26:26,042
and he made it seem like you were
maybe approaching him as well.

567
00:26:26,126 --> 00:26:27,752
Okay, but did I know him first?

568
00:26:27,836 --> 00:26:29,337
No, you didn't know him first.

569
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:31,840
But how do you know that?
What if he's lying to you?

570
00:26:31,923 --> 00:26:33,383
He's not lying to me.

571
00:26:33,466 --> 00:26:36,219
I have been working with him for months,
and you came back,

572
00:26:36,303 --> 00:26:37,637
you had a conversation with him,

573
00:26:37,721 --> 00:26:40,890
and that's when it got brought up that you
worked at the same brokerage that I did.

574
00:26:41,933 --> 00:26:43,810
Oh, God. Ah!

575
00:26:44,769 --> 00:26:46,354
[cheering]

576
00:26:46,438 --> 00:26:50,400
My first reaction was, you know,
how unprofessional,

577
00:26:50,483 --> 00:26:51,818
-how disrespectful, you know--
-Mm-hmm.

578
00:26:51,901 --> 00:26:54,654
Business is business. Money is money.
That's and important thing.

579
00:26:54,738 --> 00:26:57,449
I know that.
I'm saying maybe he's the problem.

580
00:26:57,532 --> 00:27:00,368
Why would he approach me and tell me
that you approached him?

581
00:27:00,452 --> 00:27:03,246
Maybe he wanted to work with me
without stepping on your toes...

582
00:27:03,330 --> 00:27:04,914
[Christine] It just doesn't make sense.

583
00:27:04,998 --> 00:27:08,084
You know how men are.
What if your client was lying?

584
00:27:08,168 --> 00:27:09,377
He's not lying.

585
00:27:09,461 --> 00:27:11,463
But then why was he talking to me then?

586
00:27:11,963 --> 00:27:14,257
-Heather, please.
-People lie.

587
00:27:14,341 --> 00:27:16,301
I just feel like you need to respect

588
00:27:16,384 --> 00:27:19,179
what's yours is yours
and what's mine is mine.

589
00:27:19,929 --> 00:27:24,142
♪ This town, this town
Gonna beat you down ♪

590
00:27:24,225 --> 00:27:26,353
♪ Are you gonna let it? ♪

591
00:27:34,152 --> 00:27:36,571
-Hey, girl.
-Hey, how are you?

592
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:38,657
Sorry for being late. Traffic.

593
00:27:38,740 --> 00:27:40,742
-Oh, no. It's okay.
-You know how it is.

594
00:27:40,825 --> 00:27:43,370
-Thank you so much for meeting me.
-Of course!

595
00:27:43,453 --> 00:27:46,456
Just wanted to kind of like sit down
with you one-on-one

596
00:27:46,539 --> 00:27:48,583
and ask you a couple questions
just because, like,

597
00:27:48,667 --> 00:27:50,460
you guys have all
known each other so long--

598
00:27:50,543 --> 00:27:53,380
Seriously, it's like high school right?
And we're too old for that shit.

599
00:27:53,463 --> 00:27:56,299
[chuckles] I know.
So it's like a fine balance.

600
00:27:56,383 --> 00:27:58,176
-Yeah.
-Sometimes...

601
00:27:58,760 --> 00:28:01,012
I just feel like Christine
goes a little too far.

602
00:28:01,096 --> 00:28:03,014
Yeah. She has no filter.

603
00:28:03,098 --> 00:28:05,767
Like, whatever she thinks she just says.

604
00:28:05,850 --> 00:28:08,228
Well, I was one of the first girls
who joined the office.

605
00:28:08,311 --> 00:28:10,480
Mary and Christine used to be roommates,

606
00:28:10,563 --> 00:28:12,232
and they were kind of like one unit,

607
00:28:12,315 --> 00:28:15,527
so I didn't feel like she was trying
to make too much effort

608
00:28:15,610 --> 00:28:17,987
-to, you know, become friends with me.
-Yeah.

609
00:28:18,071 --> 00:28:19,697
Uh, but it took time.

610
00:28:20,365 --> 00:28:21,533
Probably two years.

611
00:28:21,616 --> 00:28:23,535
-Two years?
-Yeah.

612
00:28:23,618 --> 00:28:25,870
-Oh, my God.
-I know.

613
00:28:25,954 --> 00:28:28,665
-But I feel like now she's--
-I have a long road ahead of me.

614
00:28:28,748 --> 00:28:31,751
-I know. [chuckles]
-Are you feeling okay after last night?

615
00:28:31,835 --> 00:28:34,671
I'm feeling good.
I mean, actually, I didn't really drink.

616
00:28:34,754 --> 00:28:36,131
How did you get out of that?

617
00:28:36,214 --> 00:28:37,382
I had water.

618
00:28:37,465 --> 00:28:39,676
-Oh, my God, I should've done that.
-I know.

619
00:28:39,759 --> 00:28:42,220
-You dumped it out and put water in it?
-Okay.

620
00:28:42,303 --> 00:28:43,555
I was trying to say no,

621
00:28:43,638 --> 00:28:45,598
and I don't think Christine
was having any of that.

622
00:28:45,682 --> 00:28:48,560
-Christine was pushing you hard for that.
-So I'm paying for it today.

623
00:28:48,643 --> 00:28:51,479
I know. I mean, I wanted to drink,

624
00:28:51,563 --> 00:28:54,357
but I think I might be pregnant.

625
00:28:54,816 --> 00:28:55,692
Oh, my God!

626
00:28:55,775 --> 00:28:57,777
-Yeah.
-When do you know?

627
00:28:58,361 --> 00:29:00,864
Well, I'm late, and...

628
00:29:00,947 --> 00:29:02,615
Oh, my god, that's so exciting!

629
00:29:02,699 --> 00:29:04,409
You guys had been trying
for a while, right?

630
00:29:04,492 --> 00:29:07,871
We've been trying. I mean,
the thing is I had two miscarriages.

631
00:29:07,954 --> 00:29:10,290
So nobody really knows,

632
00:29:10,373 --> 00:29:15,044
but I'm just trying to keep it on the low
until, uh, I figure out if it's safe,

633
00:29:15,128 --> 00:29:16,546
but it's very, very early.

634
00:29:16,629 --> 00:29:18,798
-I will send you all the positive...
-Thank you.

635
00:29:18,882 --> 00:29:21,593
-...good vibes, keep my fingers crossed.
-Please, please, please.

636
00:29:21,676 --> 00:29:23,303
-Yes, of course.
-So, we'll see.

637
00:29:27,140 --> 00:29:29,142
♪ Come to life ♪

638
00:29:33,021 --> 00:29:34,731
-[knock on door]
-Hi, babe.

639
00:29:34,814 --> 00:29:37,901
You live in Hollywood. You shouldn't
leave your door open like that.

640
00:29:37,984 --> 00:29:39,527
[laughs] Hey, how are you?

641
00:29:39,861 --> 00:29:43,114
-How are you, Princess Layla?
-Good. Thanks.

642
00:29:43,198 --> 00:29:45,158
-How was your day?
-[Mary] It was good.

643
00:29:47,202 --> 00:29:49,788
Um, this might... [chuckles]

644
00:29:49,871 --> 00:29:53,208
I need to clean off the lip of this thing.
It's like the dishwasher.

645
00:29:53,291 --> 00:29:55,335
I see lipstick on those glasses already.

646
00:29:55,418 --> 00:29:57,420
I feel like I'm in a Cheesecake Factory.

647
00:29:57,504 --> 00:30:02,217
No, it's from the--
It's from the dishwasher, I promise.

648
00:30:02,300 --> 00:30:03,510
[chuckles]

649
00:30:03,593 --> 00:30:05,970
I mean, that's why you're supposed
to hand wash wine glasses,

650
00:30:06,054 --> 00:30:08,306
but I'm lazy and I don't.
You wanna sit down?

651
00:30:08,389 --> 00:30:09,682
Yeah, let's take a seat.

652
00:30:10,934 --> 00:30:12,101
Come on, Zelly.

653
00:30:15,522 --> 00:30:17,398
All right, so here, come here.

654
00:30:17,482 --> 00:30:19,567
Show me this side.
What's going on with this?

655
00:30:19,651 --> 00:30:22,654
-I just was feeling very harajuku.
-This is crazy.

656
00:30:22,737 --> 00:30:24,072
-Wish I had chopsticks.
-Hara what?

657
00:30:24,155 --> 00:30:25,740
Harajuku. Harajuku Girls.

658
00:30:25,823 --> 00:30:28,159
-It's cute. It's you. It's fitting.
-Thanks.

659
00:30:28,952 --> 00:30:30,954
Hi, Zelda. Come sit down.

660
00:30:31,538 --> 00:30:35,500
So tell me about the other night.
Like, at the party.

661
00:30:35,583 --> 00:30:39,963
I thought we were having
a really good time, and, um...

662
00:30:40,046 --> 00:30:41,422
I got some tension from Heather.

663
00:30:41,506 --> 00:30:44,092
We're fighting with each other.
We were talking about

664
00:30:44,175 --> 00:30:48,805
a client that had approached me and told
me that Heather was trying to poach him.

665
00:30:48,888 --> 00:30:52,058
And I told her, I said,
"That's really unprofessional,

666
00:30:52,141 --> 00:30:54,060
and I think poorly of you for doing that."

667
00:30:54,143 --> 00:30:55,603
It's like real estate 101.

668
00:30:55,687 --> 00:30:57,897
I think it really hurt her feelings
that I said that.

669
00:30:57,981 --> 00:31:00,400
But you were just like kind of...
You were on one.

670
00:31:00,859 --> 00:31:02,610
You and your, like, little devil horns.

671
00:31:02,694 --> 00:31:07,824
Honestly, I'm tired
of filtering myself and apologizing.

672
00:31:07,907 --> 00:31:11,744
I'm just like-- I don't even know
how to describe this. I'm just like...

673
00:31:12,245 --> 00:31:15,290
Oh, don't wanna offend this person.
Oh, don't wanna--

674
00:31:15,373 --> 00:31:16,749
It's like I'm a news anchor.

675
00:31:16,833 --> 00:31:18,710
It's like what the fuck?
I didn't sign up for this.

676
00:31:18,793 --> 00:31:21,462
I gotta be so careful about
what I say around people?

677
00:31:21,546 --> 00:31:23,673
It's like Jesus, you know?
It's just like--

678
00:31:23,756 --> 00:31:26,968
I just want to say whatever the fuck
I want and no one to get offended.

679
00:31:27,677 --> 00:31:29,095
Is that so much to ask?

680
00:31:29,178 --> 00:31:31,723
We're a badass crew to hang out with,
you know?

681
00:31:31,806 --> 00:31:34,934
-It, like, takes a special type.
-Yeah, you have to have thick skin.

682
00:31:35,018 --> 00:31:37,812
Bottom line, you're a professional.
Act like a professional.

683
00:31:37,896 --> 00:31:40,857
You have to prove that you're serious
about your job like the rest of us.

684
00:31:40,940 --> 00:31:42,692
By showing that you don't have a backbone,

685
00:31:42,775 --> 00:31:45,528
you're just wishing and hoping
it will go away. Doesn't work like that.

686
00:31:45,612 --> 00:31:47,405
I just don't respect her.

687
00:31:47,488 --> 00:31:51,367
♪ Nothing's gonna slow me down ♪

688
00:31:51,451 --> 00:31:53,828
♪ There's a beautiful day ♪

689
00:31:53,911 --> 00:31:55,663
♪ Headed your way ♪

690
00:31:55,747 --> 00:31:59,542
♪ Keep your head up, up, up
You'll be okay ♪

